<title>SWITZERLAND: UBS Private Banking most profitable division.</title>
<headline>UBS Private Banking most profitable division.</headline>
<dateline>ZURICH 1997-08-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>Profits from Union Bank of Switzerland's (UBS ) Private Banking and Institutional Asset Management division accounted for more than half of the group's net profit in the first half of 1997 and is by far the most profitable division.</p>
<p>UBS released a detailed picture of the performance of its four core businesses with results presented as if each division were a business unit operating independently in the market.</p>
<p>For this reason each division is allocated a share of equity capital and tax liabilities, UBS said in its half-year statement.</p>
<p>UBS provided following details without a comparison. Figures are in millions of Swiss francs.</p>
<p> Divisions:	    Income   Expenses  Pre-Tax    Net	ROE</p>
<p>						    Profit     Profit</p>
<p>Private Banking</p>
<p>and Institutional</p>
<p> Asset Management    2,364    1,095     1,264	1,000    n/a</p>
<p>Corporate and</p>
<p>Institutional</p>
<p> Finance		 1,673    983	 574	  474	9.5</p>
<p>Trading and sales</p>
<p> Risk Mgmt Service   2,039    1,530     509	  365	13.0</p>
<p>Retail Business</p>
<p> Switzerland	   592	608	 32 loss    26 loss  -2.7</p>
<p> Residual Results    99	 145	 64 loss    43	 n/a</p>
<p> Total		   6,767    4,361     2,251	1,856    16.4</p>
<p>-- Zurich Editorial +41 1 631 7340</p>
